le and interested in breaking it down. No pressure, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/626312-open-development-where-is-it-at-right-now-and-what-do-you-want-to-see-soon?p=629863#post629863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I like the flavour of the line, if your not comfortable with it for some personal reason, I understand and you shouldn't do use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Omegaphallic speaks for me, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T08:47:06-07:00","id":629971,"title":"","content":"And oh, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/620401-new-kith-feedback-requested\">make this happen!<br /> <br /> Please with the sugar on top?</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T12:33:14-07:00","id":630150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/626312-open-development-where-is-it-at-right-now-and-what-do-you-want-to-see-soon?p=629439#post629439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have a complicated relationship with that terminology. If people want, I can unpack it. But I'm not really in a place to debate about it, or stand and defend it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. Of course. You're the developer. You do as you wish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T09:22:06-07:00","id":631258,"title":"","content":"On the topic of what I'd like to see next, when Dave's in a position to share... After rolling it around, I'd have to go with the Huntsmen. They've grown on me some -- seeing the concept for an example Toronto Huntsman helped and I'm intrigued by whatever Yearning is -- but I don't think I'm sold on them just yet. Learning more may not change my tune, but I'd like to find out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T10:14:24-07:00","id":631281,"title":"","content":"Are Hobgoblins still confined to the Hedge, or can they enter to the human world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T14:51:11-07:00","id":631572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/626312-open-development-where-is-it-at-right-now-and-what-do-you-want-to-see-soon?p=628205#post628205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's possible there have been changes, but in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline\">the outline</a>, Dave laid out his plan.<br /> <br /> Instead of each Contract consisting of 5 powers to be bought in order, each Contract is one power, with an experience cost relative to its dot rating. They aim to revisit all/most of 1e's, but part of the idea is to nix those that are lame or redundant. No doubt when revisiting older Contract powers, they'll buff/nerf/rework stuff so it feels like a worthwhile purchase for its cost. For Universal Contracts (most of them, aside from Court and Goblin varieties), each Contract has one or more Favored Seemings, for which they do something extra. If you're a member of a Favored Seeming, you get its respective perk for free when you buy the Contract; for a Seeming not your own, you can pay 1 experience to learn the associated perk from a member of that Seeming.<br /> <br /> I think it's going in the right direction. I'd be interested in seeing some samples -- or hearing if things changed in any way -- but I'm in no rush.<br /> <br /> Hmm... Though a logistical question does have me curious. If this is still the plan, I wonder how Seemings published after the core book will work with Contract Favored Seemings. I guess it would just be a matter of, after the Seeming's main write-up, listing any Contracts for which it's a Favored Seeming and what those extra perks do. Always cool to get new powers -- especially when they can breathe extra life into published Contracts -- though I wonder if it's possible to avoid needing to cross-reference multiple books.<br /> <br /> On a similar note, I guess also amended to the 7th/8th Seeming write-up will be some examples of Kiths as flavored by that Seeming. I enjoyed those in the initial sample we got, so even more of them after the core book certainly wouldn't disappoint me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does sounds like it's going to be better than it was, but it's just an outline and as such very vague. I wonder if there's any chance we could get something akin to the Unleashings of DA: Fae?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T17:51:11-07:00","id":631776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/626312-open-development-where-is-it-at-right-now-and-what-do-you-want-to-see-soon?p=631281#post631281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Hobgoblins still confined to the Hedge, or can they enter to the human world?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hobgoblins have never, as an umbrella grouping, been confined to the Hedge. Some hobgoblins can range abroad and some cannot, but Earthside Goblin Markets have always been a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T18:03:15-07:00","id":631788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/626312-open-development-where-is-it-at-right-now-and-what-do-you-want-to-see-soon?p=631258#post631258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the topic of what I'd like to see next, when Dave's in a position to share... After rolling it around, I'd have to go with the Huntsmen. They've grown on me some -- seeing the concept for an example Toronto Huntsman helped and I'm intrigued by whatever Yearning is -- but I don't think I'm sold on them just yet. Learning more may not change my tune, but I'd like to find out.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the reason I haven't shown them yet, honestly, is that the first drafts aren't exactly what I wanted. That was partly my fault, and actually partly intentional. I wanted to see how the first drafts turned out, and what the authors came up with. Also, I had one author drop on that section.<br /> <br /> Since that started, I've come up with a lot of new ideas, also I've caught a couple of cool ideas from these forums. So, I want to get them into a presentation I think is worth sharing before I share them. Right now, it'd be unfair to share them, because they look nothing like what I want to see them as in the final version of the product.<br /> <br /> Basically, once I get second drafts, I'll share them.<br /> <br /> They're totally a thing I'm excited to share.<br /> <br /> Partly, I chose the Huntsmen because I felt they were a thing I could really run wild with, and do something new and interesting, and bring an exciting new dimension to the game. But, that takes a little growth, evolution, and development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T19:00:51-07:00","id":631822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/626312-open-development-where-is-it-at-right-now-and-what-do-you-want-to-see-soon?p=629939#post629939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always like hearing where people are coming from, if you'd be comfortable and interested in breaking it down. No pressure, though.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sure sure. Excuse the stream-of-consciousness spew here.<br /> <br /> The short and long of it is, my mother is a non-functioning schizophrenic. My father fought in Vietnam, and had severe PTSD. I have a few significant issues of my own (without getting specific, because that can cause my family issues) I grew up with extreme examples of mental illness all around me. I dealt with words like madness, psycho, schizo, crazy, and not only were they hurtful, they were universally dismissive of the humanity. My parents weren't people; they were &quot;crazies&quot;. I wasn't a teenager, I was &quot;a risk to myself and others&quot;. We got defined by these things, and never by people that wanted to help, but always people that wanted to file us away and do their best to close their eyes.<br /> <br /> Madness, as a concept, is complex, and has a strained relationship with oppressive politics. It disproportionately affected women, minorities, and poor people, and was used as an umbrella description for any number of issues. Most importantly though, it was an excuse for unwilling captivity. It was an excuse to imprison damaged people.<br /> <br /> Most modern concepts of madness spring from those archaic ideas, and in games, primarily Lovecraft. Madness was something that privileged white men experienced when they had to face something outside their comfortable bubble. Unfortunately, there's just no good way to use the concept in madness without coming off as insensitive or condescending, because it's not really one thing; it's a dismissive concept used to blanket a great number of issues, and simplify them to the point of meaninglessness.<br /> <br /> You can see this evidenced in portrayals of Malkavians over the years. Often, their &quot;madness&quot; was a joke. Often, it was &quot;scary&quot;. You'd hear people say, &quot;Malkavians are great, but only when they're done right.&quot; Nobody agrees when that is. But most importantly, &quot;madness&quot; defined them. There's no way to &quot;do it right&quot; when mental illness is the single feature that defines a person. That, to me, is inherently &quot;doing it wrong&quot;. You cannot &quot;do it right&quot; so long as what you're doing is diminishing a person's identity in favour of one trait. This is doubly important when it's one trait that's NOT actually congruent from person to person.<br /> <br /> If I'm going to touch on mental illness, and I most certainly am because it's important to me, the least I can do is give it the respect of specificity. It's never a punishment. It's never a consequence of being a &quot;bad person&quot;. It's why I fought tooth and nail to get &quot;Derangements&quot; removed from the Storytelling System.<br /> <br /> Games, to me, are about what you do, not about the state you're in. They're about actions and consequences; trappings like mental illness are not actions, they influence actions. You can certainly act in response to mental illness. So my description of a game is never going to focus on things that have happened to you; it's always about things you are doing, and things you are experiencing and engaging with actively.<br /> <br /> Also, frankly, Changeling never really delivered on the promise of &quot;madness&quot;. You can't really call it &quot;madness&quot; when everything is really quite literal. You're not &quot;seeing things&quot; if the dragon in front of you can actually eat you. You're just dealing with being able to see very real dragons.<br /> <br /> Changeling is not a game about unwilling captivity. Characters in Changeling are not unwilling captives. They <b>were</b> unwilling captives. To me, dealing with these issues and building a new life is significantly more compelling than wallowing in them. Changeling is a game of Beautiful Lies, and Bittersweet Truths. It's a game about sometimes choosing to embrace lies, because they're prettier and softer than the truth. And it's sometimes about choosing to embrace the truth, despite the fact that the truth won't comfort you just by virtue of being the truth. It's about wondering if people actually care when they tell you they understand, or if they're just trying to brush you under the rug. It's about telling the truth, and facing people willing to blame you for your victimisation. It's about that crushing fucking moment when you wonder if it's even worth telling yourself the truth, because you might blame yourself for the awful shit that happened. It's about choking down the truth when you threw up last night, because even though your loved ones care, telling them the truth is just going to mean more uncomfortable questions. It's about escaping Arcadia, and coming back to this boring shithole. It's about wondering if maybe you were better off staying there, then it's about beating yourself up because WHY THE FUCK WOULD YOU THINK THAT.<br /> <br /> Changeling isn't a game about madness. It's a game about whether or not the truth is worth it. Because the truth hurts, and there's no escaping that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":70,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","user":"MachineIV","date":". 08-18-2015, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":24}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T22:56:22-07:00","id":631984,"title":"","content":"A Storytelling Game of Preternatural Lucidity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T23:49:48-07:00","id":632023,"title":"","content":"David, I feel you in more ways than one (so I hope you will excuse the random rumblings that follow). My family has consistently been plagued by war, revolution, crisis, and the marks these leave on the psyche and the family and community's shared unconsciousness. I am myself currently undergoing psychoanalysis, after I almost went catatonic a couple of years ago.<br /> <br /> I have to agree with you that Derangements and the old Morality/Humanity system felt...very Victorian. It fit early nWoD but only in a caricature-esque. That said, I think that <i>unfortunately</i>, a single event (let alone a series of events in the slightly-darker-than-our-own WoD) can indeed affect you in ways that, at some point or another, feel unbearable. Someone struggling with depression faces the very real, very defining fight to get out of bed and do something, even if just for today. Even if tomorrow's struggle has already been lost. The stigma associated with mental illness survives and thrives today, even when people more broken than you are the ones looking at you and thinking &quot;that's a lost soul if I ever saw one, and I want nothing to do with them&quot;. In this regard, I liked cWoD's flaw system, in that it allowed for characters to carry their personal scars into the present story. And by like, I mean it helped me deal with personal, psyche-related issues. It can be very distressing, not just to have grown up with mental illness and then see someone roleplay Malkavians recklessly, but also with a guilted sexuality, or a multi-ethnic background in a pretty much &quot;homogeneous&quot; (not really, but since the history textbooks say so, most people believe the official story) European country, to face a racist, sexist elder that can turn you to dust just because his mastery of Auspex allows him to see that the WoD is in fact a roleplaying game and you're the player behind the character, and he doesn't like you (I put a funny little hyperbole here).<br /> <br /> That's what fascinates me with roleplaying games. The actions and choices, like you said. It helped me accept myself for who I am to such an extent that I am almost addicted to roleplaying (Vampire, mostly) at times of stress or crisis.<br /> <br /> Now, on Malkavians, well... I like them. Having been the psychologically troubled (but ridiculously harmless) kid at school, it entertains that side of me that wanted to joke with people's weird, funny little looks. Yeah, fishmalks are distasteful (although, a friend of mine suffering with mental illness enjoys playing them immensely), but doing them right for me means using to your advantage that single trait other Vampires would use to step all over you. If Dementation allowed them to remove any and all mental illness from their psyche, I personally would only want to gain control <i>over</i> my issues, not eclipse them. Like the stories about how certain kinds of mental illness are actually a different perspective on reality... Violent outbursts notwithstanding, de-stigmatised mental illness would actually be a totally different story. That's the reason, I suppose, why the Magician tarot card reversed symbolises both the Magus and mental illness. That's what Malkavians felt like to me, I guess.<br /> <br /> So I enjoyed playing them in the same way I enjoy the feeling of relief after I come out of my psychoanalytic sessions, even though they can be tense and almost traumatic at times. I could simply remove elements I consider sensitive from my games entirely, protecting myself from having to Storytell or roleplay uncomfortably close to home scenarios. But that feels too much like how contemporary psychology and psychiatry approaches mental illness today, treating symptoms rather than causes. To quote Sigmund, &quot;<span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Unexpressed emotions will never die. They are buried alive and will come forth later in uglier ways.&quot; and &quot;</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Out of your vulnerabilities will come your strength.&quot;</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">.<br /> <br /> Apologies if my thoughts on how roleplaying has been therapeutic for me were insensitive or poorly expressed.<br /> <br /> Edit: Your description of Changeling sealed the deal for me. Once 2nd ed. is out, I'm definitely giving it a try!</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":59,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","user":"stylanski","date":". 08-19-2015, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T00:17:50-07:00","id":632038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/626312-open-development-where-is-it-at-right-now-and-what-do-you-want-to-see-soon?p=631822#post631822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's about choking down the truth when you threw up last night, because even though your loved ones care, telling them the truth is just going to mean more uncomfortable questions. It's about escaping Arcadia, and coming back to this boring shithole. It's about wondering if maybe you were better off staying there, then it's about beating yourself up because WHY THE FUCK WOULD YOU THINK THAT.<br /> <br /> Changeling isn't a game about madness. It's a game about whether or not the truth is worth it. Because the truth hurts, and there's no escaping that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Fucking yes!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T19:45:39-07:00","id":632971,"title":"","content":"Wow that was just powerful. Society does need to do more for mental illness.<br /> <br /> I think that part of why most people react to mental illness like that is out of fear, fear that they don't know if this person might try and hurt them, fear of the greater unpredictablity of behavior, fear that it could be them, ect...<br /> <br /> And sometimes a sense of powerlessness as well.<br /> <br /> I have drug addicts for parents, with all the fucked up shit that comes with that. I have my own mental health, occasional suicidal thoughts, also I have brain damage at birth so I can be odd at times.<br /> <br /> I like Lovecraftian horror because it faces the horrors of both mental illness and the pain from a universal that makes no fucking sense, the universal is the real horror story, the genre is really just our way of coping with that essential truth. <br /> <br /> Changeling feels like Lovecraftian horrors mascerading as Folk Tales inspired figures, because the True Fae are simple too alien to interact with reality unfiltered, they simply don't understand it, reality to them is as alien as they are to it, so they draw legends and fantasies around them like a cloak, as interface to interact with reality, as we know.<br /> <br /> Lovecraftian Faery Tales.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T05:42:03-07:00","id":636909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/626312-open-development-where-is-it-at-right-now-and-what-do-you-want-to-see-soon?p=631822#post631822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I'm going to touch on mental illness, and I most certainly am because it's important to me, the least I can do is give it the respect of specificity. It's never a punishment. It's never a consequence of being a &quot;bad person&quot;. It's why I fought tooth and nail to get &quot;Derangements&quot; removed from the Storytelling System.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you David, removing Derangements from the game was one of the best features IMO. Coming from a similar background (with relatives subject to different forms of schizophrenia), I totally share your thoughts. Mental health is generally treated in RPG as a biological or individual feature, when it's something complex (one is not another), something with a strong social definition (look at the handicap : being blind would not be a problem in a society of blind people, because the whole social institutions would be built upon the premise that everybody's blind), and something with strong social implications. So it's cool to see how these things are taken in account by producers of culture as you.<br /> <br /> I have a question that has nothing to do with this. Here it is : As Changeling are escaping with fear of being taken back, why are they staying near the hedge? Wouldn't it be the first locations to avoid?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/824-araknee","name":"Araknee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T06:44:26-07:00","id":636934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Araknee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/626312-open-development-where-is-it-at-right-now-and-what-do-you-want-to-see-soon?p=636909#post636909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you David, removing Derangements from the game was one of the best features IMO. Coming from a similar background (with relatives subject to different forms of schizophrenia), I totally share your thoughts. Mental health is generally treated in RPG as a biological or individual feature, when it's something complex (one is not another), something with a strong social definition (look at the handicap : being blind would not be a problem in a society of blind people, because the whole social institutions would be built upon the premise that everybody's blind), and something with strong social implications. So it's cool to see how these things are taken in account by producers of culture as you.<br /> <br /> I have a question that has nothing to do with this. Here it is : As Changeling are escaping with fear of being taken back, why are they staying near the hedge? Wouldn't it be the first locations to avoid?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot of reasons. First off, goblin fruit is super nice to have. Also, it's a path into dreams, which is a thing for Changelings now (Oneiromancy will be tied to paths in the Hedge). <br /> <br /> Also, your Icon is in the Hedge; that scrap of yourself you left behind. It's the best way for a Huntsman to find you. It's smart to dig it out and keep it safe. Even if in time, it'll disappear and end up back in the Hedge again. You can never fully separate that part of you from the Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T10:42:46-07:00","id":637165,"title":"","content":"I have the feeling that The Hedge supplemental book will explain better why a Changeling would want to go into the Hedge. Also Goblin Markets.<br /> <br /> Oneiromancy sounds like its under gone some really exciting changes, it and pledges are what I'm looking forward to most right now.<br /> <br /> Does going along paths in the Hedge to get to dreams mean that the Skien has merged with the Hedge now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T10:47:10-07:00","id":637169,"title":"","content":"Let's just say that the Goblin Minors makes more sense.<br /> <br /> I definitely have appreciated what was done with Oneiromancy and the Hedge. It's way more accessible and pertinent to the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-23-2015, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T12:13:39-07:00","id":637250,"title":"","content":"Goblin Miners and Succubi/Cambion childern did mark a shift in thinking when it comes to the barrier between the physical world and the dream world, which aside from a critical failure on cobblethought, was very solid, had become something physical things, including creatures could enter and exit (Goblin Miner could come and go, and Cambion childern could be born to a Succubus mom, and then sent to the father in the material world via the hedge), so that already hinted at the coming approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T12:28:00-07:00","id":637262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/626312-open-development-where-is-it-at-right-now-and-what-do-you-want-to-see-soon?p=637169#post637169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's just say that the Goblin Minors makes more sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, those adult Goblins must have come from somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-23-2015, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T12:31:15-07:00","id":637263,"title":"","content":"When a young person starts feeling very special changes...<br /> <br /> (Doh. Miners, not minors)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-24-2015, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T18:57:17-07:00","id":637627,"title":"","content":"Ha, don't worry, the internet is no place for proper spelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link"